  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "On November 1, 2026, a privately owned Learjet 60 business jet crashed in Palm Beach County, Florida, while en route from Austin–Bergstrom International Airport in Texas to North Eleuthera Airport in the Bahamas.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383972939:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "John I. Leonard Community High School, a public school near the crash site, was closed on November 2 while emergency crews and investigators kept working in the area.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383972939:27"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "At a press briefing on November 2, NTSB board member Tom Chapman said investigators had found indications that the aircraft may have begun breaking apart before impact, so components could lie some distance away.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383972939:35"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The flight set out from Austin–Bergstrom International Airport, bound for North Eleuthera Airport.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383972939:origin",
        "wiki:box:1383972939:destination"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:32Z",
      "text": "It came down about 1,760 km from Austin–Bergstrom International Airport in a straight line, with about 370 km still to go.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383972939:origin",
        "wiki:box:1383972939:destination",
        "wiki:box:1383972939:coordinates"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:40Z",
      "text": "The aircraft crashed en route, and the record lists an in-flight structural failure as the summary, with the investigation still under way.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383972939:summary"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:49Z",
      "text": "The aircraft was a Learjet 60, manufactured by Bombardier Aerospace, a type that first flew in 1990.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383972939:aircraft",
        "wd:Q1267393:P176",
        "wd:Q1267393:P606"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:53Z",
      "text": "It was operated by Aurora Aviation, doing business as Upper Jets.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383972939:operator"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:58Z",
      "text": "All 9 people on board died, 7 passengers and 2 crew, according to the article.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383972939:occupants",
        "wiki:box:1383972939:fatalities",
        "wiki:box:1383972939:passengers",
        "wiki:box:1383972939:crew",
        "wiki:box:1383972939:survivors"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:06Z",
      "text": "On the ground, 1 person was injured.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383972939:ground-injuries"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:15Z",
      "text": "The aircraft departed Austin–Bergstrom International Airport at 10:37 EST (15:37 UTC).",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:timeline:1383972939:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:22Z",
      "text": "At 12:48 EST (17:48 UTC), the first officer radioed a “mayday” call to air traffic control, reporting a deteriorating situation.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:timeline:1383972939:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:31Z",
      "text": "The Palm Beach County Sheriff's Office closed Military Trail near the impact site to support the emergency response and investigation.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:investigation:1383972939:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:38Z",
      "text": "Thunderstorms were affecting the Palm Beach area around the time of the crash, with visibility of 2 to 10 mi and surface wind gusts of 20 to 30 mph.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:investigation:1383972939:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:45Z",
      "text": "According to recorded air traffic control communications, the crew reported light clear icing and moderate turbulence at about 35,000 ft, with altitude fluctuations of up to 700 ft.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:investigation:1383972939:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:53Z",
      "text": "152,110 people read the article on 2 November 2026, and it had no readers in the 8 to 60 days before, since it is a new article.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:2026_Greenacres_Learjet_60_crash:2026-11-02",
        "views:en:2026_Greenacres_Learjet_60_crash:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:02:00Z",
      "text": "The article was read in 7 languages, and after English, the most readers were in Russian, with 7,952.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:2026_Greenacres_Learjet_60_crash:2026-11-02",
        "views:ru:Катастрофа_Learjet_60_в_Гринэйкрсе:2026-11-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:02:07Z",
      "text": "On the globe, each language glows where it is mainly spoken, brighter for more readers, and a language is not a country.",
      "cites": [
